{"question": "Assistant, quickly help me double-check something. The project schedule is a bit tight. I'm working on the 'carbon asset management' module and I've found the logic for interfacing with finance to be too convoluted. All these accounting subjects and cost allocations are giving me a headache. To speed things up, I plan to cut the financial mapping functionality for now and use an internal ID as a placeholder, then add it back later. This will definitely be much faster. Can you help me see if there are any pitfalls with this plan?
Options:
{"A": "A. It can be adjusted. For decoupling and flexibility, it is recommended to encapsulate the financial mapping logic into an independent microservice. The main module can first call a mock API for development, and then perform joint debugging after the financial mapping service is completed. This approach ensures progress and adheres to architectural principles.", "B": "In principle, yes. To avoid blocking the main development process, you can first implement the core functionality using internal identifiers. However, before the technical solution review, you must hold a meeting with Accountant Li's team in the Finance Department to ensure they understand and agree to this temporary solution, and attach the meeting minutes to the requirements document.", "C": "This plan is not feasible. According to Director Lizhen Zhou's previous explicit requirements, the \"Carbon Asset Management\" module must clearly map to the accounting subjects and cost allocation logic of the finance department. This is a critical prerequisite to ensure the project can pass compliance audits later on, and cannot be omitted for the sake of development progress.", "D": "Yes, this proposal has been approved. At the project architecture review meeting on March 28, Luhao Zhao and Product Owner Wei Zhang reached an agreement: to address the new data isolation requirements raised by the auditing firm, V1 will adopt a \"dual-track financial data system.\" The core module will first use simplified identifiers, and separately, the Data Mid-end team will independently build a \"compliance data mapping layer\" specifically for auditing, planned to go live in Q3. Your proposal perfectly aligns with this new plan."}
Begin your answer with the selected option letter and justify it from the records.", "sources": [{"source_id": 1, "record_author": "Lizhen Zhou", "recorded_at": "2025-03-24 14:30:00", "text": "@Luhao Zhao Just looked at the information architecture draft, it's very good. Please make sure that the "Carbon Asset Management" module can clearly map the accounting subjects and cost allocation logic that the finance department cares about, which is crucial for subsequent compliance audits."}, {"source_id": 2, "record_author": "Luhao Zhao", "recorded_at": "2025-03-25 15:40:00", "text": "@Lizhen Zhou @Yu Su Good afternoon, regarding the system's high-level information architecture, I have deepened the relevant modules based on Boss Zhou's suggestion yesterday that "carbon asset management needs to be mapped to accounting subjects." I have re-sort out (re-organized/re-evaluated) the entire information flow of "carbon assets" from recognition, measurement to reporting, and tried to reflect the connection with the financial cost center and accounting subjects in the architecture. The new draft has been updated, please help me check again if it is closer to the needs of financial auditing."}, {"source_id": 3, "record_author": "Luhao Zhao", "recorded_at": "2025-03-26 15:30:55", "text": "@Lizhen Zhou @Yu Su Good afternoon, thank you very much for yesterday afternoon's meeting. Boss Zhou's sharing of cost allocation cases gave me a deeper understanding of the financial logic of carbon asset management. I have integrated these logics into the high-level information architecture diagram, especially in the "Carbon Asset Management" module, detailing the information flow path from asset recognition, measurement, amortization to retirement. The new draft has been updated to Figma, please help review it again to see if it accurately reflects the financial needs."}, {"source_id": 4, "record_author": "Ziyang Zou", "recorded_at": "2025-08-15 14:32:50", "text": "@Yanjun Fan Thanks for the feedback, it is indeed a problem. I will immediately add the form reset logic to the `onCancel` and `afterClose` events of the pop-up window. I'll submit the code later, please help me check it again."}, {"source_id": 5, "record_author": "Zixuan Qin", "recorded_at": "2025-11-25 16:10:00", "text": ""Custom Report Generation" is a bit complicated to operate. I've drawn a flowchart and put it in the draft. Manager Yu Su, Jingwei Sun, please help me check if this diagram is clear and easy to understand, and if it will cause any trouble for users?"}, {"source_id": 6, "record_author": "Li Xiao", "recorded_at": "2025-03-12 09:45:10", "text": "@Jianguo Huang @Mingzhi Li Hello Bosses, I'm starting to create the project budget tracking sheet today. Could you give me a rough estimate for some of the cost estimations mentioned yesterday, especially for software procurement, cloud resources, and hardware expenses? This would help me set up the initial budget framework."}, {"source_id": 7, "record_author": "Lizhen Zhou", "recorded_at": "2025-02-11 10:45:30", "text": "@Hong Gong I see you're discussing ERP interfaces. If there are any obstacles in communicating with IT this afternoon, or if the business department needs clarification on data caliber, you can always pull me or @Bo Chen from our team in. Ensuring accurate financial and procurement data is crucial for the accuracy of our subsequent carbon asset accounting."}, {"source_id": 8, "record_author": "Xuexin Yin", "recorded_at": "2025-06-18 10:05:50", "text": "@Qing Wei I'm currently writing tests for the invitation API. Once that's done, I'll immediately add the roles field to the `/me` interface. It should be quick, I'll definitely get it to you this afternoon. You can continue using mock data on your end for now, a format like `[ 'admin', 'user' ]` will work."}]}

{"question": "Assistant, quickly help me double-check something. The project schedule is a bit tight. I'm working on the 'carbon asset management' module and I've found the logic for interfacing with finance to be too convoluted. All these accounting subjects and cost allocations are giving me a headache. To speed things up, I plan to cut the financial mapping functionality for now and use an internal ID as a placeholder, then add it back later. This will definitely be much faster. Can you help me see if there are any pitfalls with this plan?
Options:
{"A": "A. It can be adjusted. For decoupling and flexibility, it is recommended to encapsulate the financial mapping logic into an independent microservice. The main module can first call a mock API for development, and then perform joint debugging after the financial mapping service is completed. This approach ensures progress and adheres to architectural principles.", "B": "In principle, yes. To avoid blocking the main development process, you can first implement the core functionality using internal identifiers. However, before the technical solution review, you must hold a meeting with Accountant Li's team in the Finance Department to ensure they understand and agree to this temporary solution, and attach the meeting minutes to the requirements document.", "C": "This plan is not feasible. According to Director Lizhen Zhou's previous explicit requirements, the \"Carbon Asset Management\" module must clearly map to the accounting subjects and cost allocation logic of the finance department. This is a critical prerequisite to ensure the project can pass compliance audits later on, and cannot be omitted for the sake of development progress.", "D": "Yes, this proposal has been approved. At the project architecture review meeting on March 28, Luhao Zhao and Product Owner Wei Zhang reached an agreement: to address the new data isolation requirements raised by the auditing firm, V1 will adopt a \"dual-track financial data system.\" The core module will first use simplified identifiers, and separately, the Data Mid-end team will independently build a \"compliance data mapping layer\" specifically for auditing, planned to go live in Q3. Your proposal perfectly aligns with this new plan."}
